{
  "analysis": "We now know DG_DrawFrame saves /tmp/frame.bmp every 10 frames using writeBMPFile with 32-bit BGRA pixels from DG_ScreenBuffer. The image header writes a standard BMP. Doom will use fopen/fwrite/fclose, which ultimately use syscall stubs for open/write/close. We need to implement a MIPS interpreter capable enough to run Doom and handle syscalls.",
  "plan": "Print the rest of doomgeneric_img.c and the syscall constants/stubs in my_stdlib.c. Then inspect the ELF entry/start code and key function disassembly to ensure the interpreter handles the required MIPS instructions and ABI.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "awk 'NR>=200 && NR<=260 {printf \"%4d %s\\n\", NR, $0}' doomgeneric/doomgeneric/doomgeneric_img.c\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "awk 'NR>=1500 && NR<=1565 {printf \"%4d %s\\n\", NR, $0}' doomgeneric/doomgeneric/my_stdlib.c\n",
      "duration": 0.1
